problem "The table below summarizes the distribution of US states based on whether they had a state-level property tax and a state-level vehicle tax in $2014$.\n\n|  | State property tax | No state property tax |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| State vehicle tax | $36$ | $3$ |\n| No state vehicle tax | $8$ | $3$ |\n\nTo the nearest tenth of a percent, what percent of states with a state-level property tax did not have a state-level vehicle tax?"] [17592186229365 :question/problem "In a community art program, participants were classified based on their age and their assigned activity group. The results are summarized in the table below.\n\n|  | Age $0-9$ | Age $10-19$ | Age $20 +$ | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Painting | $4$ | $10$ | $11$ | $25$ |\n| Sculpture | $5$ | $8$ | $7$ | $20$ |\n| Photography | $11$ | $12$ | $2$ | $25$ |\n| **Total** | **$20$** | **$30$** | **$20$** | **$70$** |\n\nOne of these participants will be selected at random. What is the probability of selecting a participant from the Painting group, given that the participant is at least $10$ years old? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)\n\nThe probability is\n{{field-1}}."] [17592186229366 :question/problem "A college student council surveyed attendees of four different campus events, asking each participant to choose one event they enjoyed most. Each survey response was received either in person or via a web form. The table below shows the distribution of preferences, in percent, by response method. The total number of web responses was three times the number of in-person responses.\n\n|  | In person | Web form |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Open mic night | $40 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $30 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| Outdoor movie | $25 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $20 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| Game tournament | $20 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $25 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| Art fair | $15 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $25 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| **Total** | **$100 \\mathrm{\\% }$** | **$100 \\mathrm{\\% }$** |\n\nIf a student who preferred the game tournament is selected at random, what is the probability that the student responded using the web form?\n\nThe probability is\n{{field-1}}."] [17592186229424 :question/problem "A museum surveyed visitors about four exhibits, asking each to choose the one they enjoyed most. Each response was submitted either at an on-site kiosk or via an email link. The table below shows the distribution of preferences, in percent, by response method. The total number of email responses was four times the number of kiosk responses.\n\n|  | Kiosk | Email |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Sculpture | $18 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $22 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| Painting | $37 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $28 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| Science | $22 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $30 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| History | $23 \\mathrm{\\% }$ | $20 \\mathrm{\\% }$ |\n| **Total** | **$100 \\mathrm{\\% }$** | **$100 \\mathrm{\\% }$** |\n\nIf a visitor who preferred the sculpture exhibit is selected at random, what is the probability that the visitor responded via email?\n\nThe probability is\n{{field-1}}."] [17592186229425 :question/problem "A cafeteria records each diner’s favorite entrée and payment method. The data is summarized in the table below.\n\n|  | Cash | Card | Mobile |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Pizza | $12$ | $18$ | $x$ |\n| Salad | $20$ | $25$ | $15$ |\n\nIf a person who preferred pizza is selected at random, the probability that the person paid by card is $\\frac{2}{5}$. What is the value of $x$?\n\n$x =$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186229426 :question/problem "An electronics shop records whether a buyer’s main purchase was a laptop or a tablet, and how the order was placed. The data is summarized in the table below.\n\n|  | In-store | Online | Phone |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Laptops | $35$ | $20$ | $12$ |\n| Tablets | $21$ | $14$ | $x$ |\n\nIf a person who bought a tablet is selected at random, the probability that the person ordered by online is $\\frac{1}{6}$. What is the value of $x$