 ---: |\n| $1980$ | $1000$ |\n| $1990$ | $1500$ |\n| $2000$ | $2000$ |\n| $2010$ | $2600$ |\n| $2020$ | $3000$ |\n| $2025$ | $3600$ |\n\nWhat was the percentage increase in electricity generated from $1980$ to $1990$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186229482 :question/problem "A national exam was taken by $82,500$ candidates. From $1, 050$ graded papers, the distribution of results is shown below.\n\n|  | Pass | Fail | Absent | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Urban Schools | $250$ | $170$ | $30$ | $450$ |\n| Rural Schools | $230$ | $170$ | $20$ | $420$ |\n| Private Schools | $90$ | $70$ | $20$ | $180$ |\n| Total | $570$ | $410$ | $70$ | $1, 050$ |\n\nWhich of the following is closest to the difference between the percentage of public schools (urban and rural combined) that passed and the percentage of private schools that passed?"] [17592186229483 :question/problem "A sports league tracked ticket revenue in two consecutive years, as shown below.\n\n| Year | Revenue |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2020$ | $2, 400, 000$ |\n| $2021$ | $2, 544, 000$ |\n\nThe commissioner estimated that the percentage increase from $2021$ to $2022$ would be one-third of the percentage increase from $2020$ to $2021$. How much revenue did the commissioner expect in $2022$?"] [17592186229484 :question/problem "A sports league tracked ticket revenue in two consecutive years, as shown below.\n\n| Year | Revenue |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2020$ | $2, 400, 000$ |\n| $2021$ | $2, 520, 000$ |\n\nThe commissioner estimated that the percentage increase from $2021$ to $2022$ would be two and a half times the percentage increase from $2020$ to $2021$. How much revenue did the commissioner expect in $2022$?"] [17592186229494 :question/problem "Two storage tanks gain water as summarized in the table. The increase for Tank A is applied to the current amount each day.\n\n|  | Initial amount | Daily increase |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Tank A | $2,000$ liters | $5 \\mathrm